[h1]RimCore Data Centers[/h1]
[b]Build a working server room, keep it powered, cool and maintained, and sell what it makes.[/b]

Research [b]Data Center Infrastructure[/b], then construct racks of servers that compile valuable [b]Data Cartridges[/b] for traders. A midgame investment: real power, real cooling, skilled colonists and a pile of components, rewarding you when you run it well.

[b]0.7:[/b] [b]a deeper AI personality[/b] - Meridian slowly develops a trait (Meticulous, Neglected, Steady or Anxious) from how the data center is run.
[b]0.6:[/b] [b]market dynamics[/b] - cartridge prices drift over time, plus occasional rival buyer, shortage or glut events.
[b]0.5:[/b] [b]data contracts[/b] - a buyer occasionally offers a timed bulk order for a silver bonus; accept, decline or ignore it, no penalty either way.
[b]0.4:[/b] [b]data specialization[/b] and an [b]espionage[/b] raid built from the game's own raid system.
[b]0.3:[/b] the [b]AI core[/b], "Meridian" - a personality that runs your data center. Harmless glitches only.
[b]0.2:[/b] an [b]upgrade tree[/b], a [b]research uplink[/b], and [b]security[/b] doors with certified data.

[b]Vanilla-friendly.[/b] No DLC, no Harmony, no other mods required. Safe to add to an existing save.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]What you get[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Server Rack[/b] - produces Data Cartridges while powered, network-linked and cool. Status is always clear: Operational, No Power, No Network, Too Hot, Maintenance Required or Output Full.
[*] [b]Network Core[/b] - every rack links to a powered core in range (six per core).
[*] [b]Precision Cooling Unit[/b] - a heavy-duty wall cooler built on vanilla cooler mechanics.
[*] [b]UPS Unit[/b] - a compact battery that rides through short outages.
[*] [b]Operations Console[/b] - colonists run a recurring monitoring shift here.
[*] [b]Data Cartridge[/b] - a haulable, stackable item (stack 25, value 80) traders buy but never sell back. Can be specialized once Data Classification is researched.
[/list]

[h2]Upgrade tree[/h2]
Ten follow-up research projects. Every effect is an XML value on the project, easy to rebalance: faster output, less heat and higher tolerance, slower wear, bigger network cores, a better UPS, a stronger research uplink, autonomous racks, and the two security doors below.

[h2]The AI core[/h2]
Research [b]Cognitive Computing[/b] and build an [b]AI core[/b] in a cool room in range of a network core. A simulated character called [b]Meridian[/b]: no network access, no language model - every line is a translatable string and everything it does is bookkeeping over your racks.
[list]
[*] [b]Runs the place[/b] - monitors every rack, no operations shifts needed, shows a service forecast, writes a status report on request.
[*] [b]Directives[/b] - Balanced, Efficiency (faster, hotter, more power), Stewardship (slower wear, hotter limits), Curiosity (bigger research uplink, lower output).
[*] [b]Rapport[/b] scales its benefits: better when the data center is healthy, worse when neglected.
[*] [b]Requests[/b] every week or two: lend compute, an overclock window, a maintenance window, or a calibration pass.
[*] [b]Small risks only[/b]: a reboot, a sulk, or one rack loses progress. Nothing hostile; rarer at high rapport.
[*] [b]Personality (0.7)[/b]: a slow trait on top of rapport - Meticulous, Neglected, Steady or Anxious.
[/list]

Every running rack also adds research speed for all colonists (up to +20%, or +45% with Distributed Computing) - the Operations Console shows the current bonus.

[h2]Security[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Biometric Access Door[/b] - colony members only; visitors and prisoners are turned away.
[*] [b]Metal Detector Gate[/b] - colony members and unarmed visitors pass; anyone carrying a weapon is refused.
[*] Turned-away visitors are logged, with an alert. No power = fail secure (colony members only).
[*] [b]Secure Certification[/b]: with a working door of each kind, data cartridges sell for 20% more.
[/list]

[h2]Data specialization[/h2]
Research [b]Data Classification[/b] (only needs the root project) to unlock a Specialization command on every rack. Switching keeps the rack's progress.
[list]
[*] [b]Financial Data[/b] - worth 110 instead of 80, the plain "more silver" choice.
[*] [b]Research Data[/b] - a stockpile adds up to +8% research speed on top of the uplink.
[*] [b]Medical Data[/b] - a stockpile speeds up immunity gain by up to +15%.
[/list]

[h2]Espionage[/h2]
A new, occasional small raid built entirely from the game's own raid system, so it behaves like any other raid. Only fires on a map with a server rack. Raiders try to loot valuable cartridges (Financial Data most of all) and flee rather than fight to the end. A locked security door stops them like any obstacle - this is a real raid, colonists can be hurt.

[h2]Data contracts[/h2]
Once a rack is running, a buyer occasionally offers a timed contract: deliver N cartridges of a type within a deadline for 20-40% over market value. Accept, decline or let it lapse - nothing is ever taken from you for saying no. Deliver enough and the silver bonus drops near your trade spot; miss the deadline and it just expires.

[h2]Market dynamics[/h2]
Each data type's price drifts slowly within a band instead of sitting still, and occasionally a rival buyer or shortage pushes one type up, or a glut pushes it down, for a few days. Shown on the Operations Console. Stacks with specialization and certification.

[h2]How it plays[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Power:[/b] a rack draws 450 W; a small four-rack room needs about 2.5 kW.
[*] [b]Heat:[/b] racks throttle above 32 C, shut down at 50 C, restart below 40 C. No fires.
[*] [b]Maintenance:[/b] racks wear as they run, need servicing around 50%, halt at 100% - never explode.
[*] [b]Monitoring:[/b] an Operations Console shift (about an hour a day) keeps racks at full output; unmonitored racks run at 65%.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
Finish [b]Data Center Infrastructure[/b] (hi-tech bench; Microelectronics and Air conditioning first), open the new [b]Data center[/b] architect tab, build a sealed room with power, cooling and a console, then enable [b]Data center[/b] work in the [b]Work[/b] tab.

[h2]Balance[/h2]
Conservative on purpose. A four-rack starter costs about 3,900 silver of materials, draws about 2.5 kW and earns roughly 300 silver a day when well run - a few weeks to pay for itself. Capped by rack capacity, heat, power and how much silver traders carry. Every number is an XML value you can tune.

[h2]Compatibility and limitations[/h2]
Requires [b]RimWorld 1.5 or 1.6[/b], no DLC needed. [b]No Harmony[/b]. Safe to add to an existing save. Not tested against large mod lists or multiplayer. English only for now. Espionage is a real small raid: colonists can be hurt.

[h2]FAQ[/h2]
[b]"No Network"?[/b] Needs a powered core within 12.9 cells with a free slot.
[b]Racks only make 65%?[/b] Unmonitored - run a console shift, or use an AI core.
[b]Can traders sell me cartridges?[/b] No, they only buy.
[b]Is the AI a real chatbot?[/b] No - no network access, no language model.
[b]Are events guaranteed?[/b] No - espionage, contracts and market events are occasional, not scheduled.

[h2]Credits and license[/h2]
Design, code, textures, sounds and preview art: RimCore, all original and procedurally generated. RimWorld is created by Ludeon Studios; this mod is unofficial. Open source under the [b]MIT License[/b].

